sentences.t:
En grant miedo se vieron por medio de la cort;
enbraçan los mantos los del Campeador,
e çercan el escaño, e fincan sobre so señor.

sentences.l:
In great fear themselves they-saw through middle of the court;
they-take-on-the-arm the mantles those of-the Campeador,
and they-surround the bench, and they-stand around their lord.

sentences.t:
Ferran[t] Gonçal[v]ez, [ifant de Carrión],
non vi[d]o allí dos alçasse, nin cámara abierta nin torre;
metiós sol esçaño, tanto ovo el pavor.

sentences.l:
Ferran[t] Gonçal[v]ez, [infante of Carrión],
not saw there where-himself he-might-hide, nor chamber open nor tower;
put-himself under-the bench, so-much he-had the terror.

sentences.t:
En esto despertó el que en buen ora naçió;
vi[d]o çercado el escaño de s[o]s buenos varones:
“Qués esto, mesnadas, o qué queredes vos?”

sentences.l:
At this awoke he who in good hour was-born;
he-sa[w] surrounded the bench by h[i]s good men:
“What-is this, household-troops, or what want you?”

sentences.t:
Quando los fallaron, assí vinieron sin color;
non vi[di]estes tal juego commo iva por la cort;
mandólo vedar mio Çid el Campeador,

sentences.l:
When them they-found, so they-came without colour;
not you-s[a]w such sport as was-going through the court;
ordered-it to-forbid my Çid the Campeador,

sentences.t:
Ellos en esto estando, don avien grant pesar,
fuerças de Marruecos Valençia vienen çercar;
en el campo de Quarto ellos fueron posar,

sentences.l:
They in this being, whereof they-had great grief,
forces of Marruecos Valençia come to-besiege;
in the field of Quarto they went to-encamp,

sentences.t:
Amos hermanos a part salidos son:
“Catamos la ganançia e la pérdida no;
ya en esta batalla a entrar abremos nos;

sentences.l:
Both brothers apart gone-out are:
“We-looked-at the gain and the loss not;
now in this battle to enter we-shall-have we;
